WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.474
Hybrid lasts longer than anyone plans,

2
00:00:02.474 --> 00:00:06.337
so it helps to name exactly what
still needs Active Directory.

3
00:00:06.337 --> 00:00:08.938
Synced users' attributes
are still written there.

4
00:00:08.938 --> 00:00:11.863
Kerberos applications
need groups written back.

5
00:00:11.863 --> 00:00:15.773
D N S, D H C P and legacy
apps keep the forest alive,

6
00:00:15.773 --> 00:00:20.713
and Windows logins to SQL
Server skip Conditional Access.

7
00:00:20.713 --> 00:00:23.850
Hybrid-joined devices still
need some domain policy.

8
00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:28.014
Moving a population's source of
authority has firm entry checks,

9
00:00:28.014 --> 00:00:31.550
and whether that move works
in G C C is still unverified.

10
00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:36.612
So retiring AD means clearing a list of
named dependencies, not reaching a date.

11
00:00:36.612 --> 00:00:37.990
Here's the checklist.
